mitted-the-jury-to-rely-on-the-same-acts-to-convict-mr-hernandez-escobar-of-count-four-and-one-of-the-other-counts)907 0 R(c-issues-pertaining-to-assignments-of-error)898 0 R(c-the-court-gave-doc-unbridled-suspicionless-access-to-mr-hernandez-escobars-home-without-authority-of-law)916 0 R(c-the-court-impermissibly-refused-to-require-a-clear-election-by-the-prosecution-or-factual-explanation-of-the-underlying-act-on-which-the-jurys-verdict-rests)912 0 R(c-the-courts-failure-to-enforce-the-constitutionally-mandated-juror-requirements-requires-reversal)904 0 R(c-the-double-jeopardy-violation-requires-remand-to-strike-mr-hernandez-escobars-conviction-in-count-four)908 0 R(d-statement-of-the-case)899 0 R(e-argument)900 0 R(f-conclusion)917 0 R]>>>>>>
